course: dictionary
lesson: 10154
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «A song thrush smashes snails on a favourite stone, called its anvil, to crack the shell.» Smashing snails and a stone anvil are about nature, so thrush here is a bird.
explain: The same word can point to something completely different. If a sentence talks about white patches in a mouth, itching, or a doctor, the word is probably a health word, not an animal. Always ask: what is the sentence about?
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you are probably right. If it sounds silly, look at the other clues or use a dictionary.
fact: A thrush is a songbird with a brown back and a spotted chest, such as the song thrush.
fact: «The American robin is a thrush, bigger than the British robin.» So robins can be thrushes too.
fact: Thrush can also mean an infection caused by a yeast, which makes white patches in the mouth or itching.
fact: Song thrushes often repeat phrases in their song, and they crack snail shells on a stone called an anvil.
fact: The thrush infection is common and can be treated, and it is often seen in babies' mouths.
exercise: «A song thrush smashes snails on a favourite stone, called its anvil.» In this sentence, what is a thrush? | *A songbird | A kind of snail | A type of fish | A white patch in the mouth
exercise: The doctor said the baby had thrush, with white patches in the mouth. What is thrush here? | *An infection caused by a yeast | A type of hedgehog | A songbird with a spotted chest | A stone for cracking shells
exercise: «Slugs feed at night, and hedgehogs, thrushes, frogs and beetles eat them.» Which of these animals is a bird? | Frog | Hedgehog | Beetle | *Thrush
test: Jayden says thrush always means a bird. Is he right? | Yes, it always means a bird | Yes, but only in spring | No, it means a big stone | *No, in health topics it can mean an infection
test: «The American robin is a thrush, bigger than the British robin, with a grey back and reddish breast.» What kind of bird is an American robin? | A kind of snail | *A kind of thrush | A kind of frog
exam: A baby has white patches in the mouth, and the nurse says it is thrush. Which meaning fits? | A stone used to crack shells | A songbird with a brown back | *An infection caused by a yeast | A type of slug
